html += '''</tbody></table>

    <img class="chart-img" src="''' + charts['mean_bar'] + '''" alt="Mean Price Bar Chart">

    <img class="chart-img" src="''' + charts['kde'] + '''" alt="Price Density Curves">

    <div class="callout">
        <strong>Key observation:</strong> E10 standard unleaded is the cheapest fuel type on average — consistent with its role as the default petrol grade since 2021 — while B7_PREMIUM and B10 command significant premiums. The price hierarchy (E10 < B7_STANDARD < E5 < B7_PREMIUM) is stable across all distribution statistics.
    </div>
</div>
'''

# Section 3: Price Spread & Market Competitiveness
html += '''
<div class="section" id="price-spread-analysis">
    <h2>3. Price Spread &amp; Market Competitiveness</h2>

    <p>Price dispersion — the extent to which consumers face different prices for the same fuel type at different forecourts — is a critical indicator of market competitiveness. Two metrics are examined: the total max−min <strong>range</strong> (capturing the full spread) and the <strong>interquartile range</strong> or IQR (the spread experienced by the middle 50% of stations, less sensitive to outliers).</p>

    <img class="chart-img" src="''' + charts['spread'] + '''" alt="Price Spread Comparison">

